## MAJ

### CORR-MAJ-001: SB-001 fix lacks test assertions for new admin/required-checks CAUTION lines

**Bug:** fix-round-11 added CAUTION log lines for enforce_admins removal + required_checks removal ack (in RESTORE_CAUTION_LINES). Existing ack-path tests don't assert the new log lines appear.

**Fix:** in tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh, extend the existing admin-enforcement ack + required-checks ack tests to grep the log file for the new CAUTION lines. Mirror the force_pushes + deletions assertion pattern.

### CORR-MAJ-002: forward-mode silently accepts restore-mode-only --i-understand-restore-* flags

**Bug:** scripts/enable-required-check.sh accepts all 5 --i-understand-restore-* flags (admin-enforcement, required-checks, signatures, force-pushes, deletions) in CLI parsing without restore-mode guard. Forward-mode invocations with these flags silently ignore them.

**Fix:** add a forward-mode mutex check after argument parsing:
```bash
if [ "$RESTORE_MODE" -eq 0 ]; then
  if [ "$ACK_RESTORE_ADMIN_REMOVAL" -eq 1 ] || [ "$ACK_RESTORE_REQUIRED_CHECKS_REMOVAL" -eq 1 ] || [ "$ACK_RESTORE_SIGNATURES_REMOVAL" -eq 1 ] || [ "$ACK_RESTORE_FORCE_PUSHES" -eq 1 ] || [ "$ACK_RESTORE_DELETIONS" -eq 1 ]; then
    echo 'error: --i-understand-restore-* flags are restore-mode-only; remove them or run with --restore <pre-state.json>' >&2
    exit 2
  fi
fi
```

### CORR-MAJ-003: no test covers forward-mode invocation with --i-understand-restore-* flags

**Fix:** add 5 forward-mode test cases (one per flag) asserting exit 2 + stderr 'restore-mode-only'.

### SB-009: ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 2 SHA-resolution example breaks on annotated tags

**Bug:** the example command in §12.8 Gate 2 returns tag-object SHA for annotated tags, not commit SHA. Operator copy-pasting gets wrong SHA. R11 SB-003 fix updated the script to handle annotated tags but didn't update the doc example.

**Fix:** in docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md §12.8 Gate 2, replace the example with a bash snippet that dereferences annotated tags:
```bash
TAG_REF_JSON="$(gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags/<tag>)"
OBJECT_TYPE="$(printf '%s' "$TAG_REF_JSON" | jq -r '.object.type')"
OBJECT_SHA="$(printf '%s' "$TAG_REF_JSON" | jq -r '.object.sha')"
if [ "$OBJECT_TYPE" = "tag" ]; then
  RELEASE_SHA="$(gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/tags/${OBJECT_SHA} --jq '.object.sha')"
else
  RELEASE_SHA="$OBJECT_SHA"
fi
echo "Release SHA: $RELEASE_SHA"
```
Add a note: 'Handles both lightweight + annotated tags defensively (R11 SB-003 fix in the script; this Gate 2 helper mirrors that.'

